# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# Without this, every path except / returns 404 in production. Not "looks
# broken" — an actual 404 from the CDN, before React ever loads. Refreshing
# any page inside the app, bookmarking /dashboard, or sending anyone a link
# to /pricing or /signup all failed. Only the homepage worked, and only
# because index.html is a real file at the root.
#
# The rule says: if the requested path doesn't match a file on disk, serve
# index.html with a 200 and let the client-side router work out the route.
# The 200 matters — a 301/302 would change the URL, and a 404 status would
# tell crawlers the page doesn't exist even while rendering it.
#
# Real files still win. The prerender step (scripts/prerender.mjs, run by
# `npm run build`) writes dist/<route>/index.html for the marketing routes,
# and Netlify serves those directly because they exist. This only catches
# what's left over — which is every authenticated app route, since those
# can't be prerendered.

# ⚠️ THE OLD DOMAIN MUST 301, NOT SERVE.
#
# eliv8os.com became the primary domain on 27 Aug. Netlify does NOT redirect a
# domain alias to the primary — only the www/apex counterpart of the primary is
# redirected for you. Verified live: leadeos.com returned `HTTP/2 200` with no
# Location header, i.e. it was serving the identical site from the same deploy.
#
# Two domains serving byte-identical pages is duplicate content, and the damage
# lands on the NEW domain — search engines pick one canonical themselves, and
# they have years of history pointing at leadeos.com and days pointing here.
#
# ⭐ This also does the job the domain was kept for: leadeos.com holds every
# indexed page, and `utm_source=chatgpt` is the only channel that has ever
# brought this product a stranger. A 301 passes that to eliv8os.com. It works
# only while the domain is still REGISTERED — letting it lapse drops the link,
# and no rule here can substitute for owning the name.
#
# ⚠️ The `!` is load-bearing: without it Netlify serves the file that exists at
# that path (index.html) instead of redirecting. And these MUST stay above the
# SPA fallback below — first match wins.
http://leadeos.com/*       https://eliv8os.com/:splat   301!
https://leadeos.com/*      https://eliv8os.com/:splat   301!
http://www.leadeos.com/*   https://eliv8os.com/:splat   301!
https://www.leadeos.com/*  https://eliv8os.com/:splat   301!

# ⚠️ Kill the retired prompt chunks.
#
# src/lib/prompts.js used to be bundled and served, so Solomon's full system
# prompt was fetchable with one unauthenticated request. It has been moved
# server-side and the current build emits no such chunk — but Netlify keeps
# assets from earlier deploys addressable, so the OLD hashed URL kept working
# and the file was still there for anyone holding the link.
#
# Removing the reference is not the same as removing the file. This is.
/assets/prompts-*    /index.html   404

/*    /index.html   200
